.TH SOLOISTD 1 "2026-09-12" "soloistd 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soloistd \- manage Spotify Soloist as a user service with automatic updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soloistd setup
.RB [ \-\-device\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-api\-key
.IR KEY ]
.br
.B soloistd run
.br
.B soloistd pair
.br
.B soloistd update
.br
.B soloistd ctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS .\|.\|.]
.br
.B soloistd service
.IR ACTION
.br
.B soloistd version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soloistd
is a supervisor for Spotify Soloist. It keeps the Soloist API key out of the
systemd unit, runs Soloist as a systemd user service, checks the official
Spotify CDN for new builds, and recovers when a build expires.
.PP
The daemon compares the official archive's CDN metadata at startup and every
six hours. When the archive changes,
.B soloistd
downloads the stable archive for the running architecture, validates it by
executing
.BR "soloist --version" ,
atomically replaces its user\-owned copy of the executable, and restarts
Soloist gracefully. A failed check never interrupts playback.
.PP
Spotify documents daemon exit status 10 as "build expired". That remains an
independent fallback: the current build is downloaded and Soloist restarted
whenever status 10 is reported, even if the metadata check failed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Configure the Spotify Connect device name and API key, then fetch Soloist. The
interactive key prompt does not echo. The default device name is
.IR soloistd@ <hostname>.
.TP
.B run
Run the supervisor in the foreground. This is what the user service starts.
.TP
.B pair
Replace the saved Spotify Connect session. Stop the installed service first,
because Soloist permits only one process per data directory.
.TP
.B update
Fetch the current official Soloist build immediately.
.TP
.B ctl
Run a
.B soloist ctl
command against the managed Soloist process.
.TP
.B service
Manage the systemd user service. The actions are
.BR install ,
.BR uninstall ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.BR restart ,
.BR status ,
and
.BR logs .
.B uninstall
removes only the unit and keeps the configuration and playback data.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SOLOIST_API_KEY
Supplies the API key to
.BR "soloistd setup" ,
keeping it out of shell history.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Locate the files below. The usual
.IR ~/.config ,
.IR ~/.local/share ,
and
.I ~/.cache
fallbacks are used when they are unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/soloistd/config.json
Private configuration, mode 0600 in a directory of mode 0700.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soloistd/bin/soloist
Managed Soloist executable.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soloistd/release.json
Metadata for the installed release.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/soloist
Spotify session and state.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/soloist
Playback cache.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/soloistd.service
Generated user unit. It contains only the path to
.BR soloistd ,
never the API key.
.SH SECURITY
The generated unit never contains the API key. Soloist itself requires the key
as a command\-line argument, so the key can still be visible to same\-user
process inspection while Soloist is running.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B soloistd
exits 0 on success, 2 on a usage error, and otherwise propagates the exit
status of the command it ran.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
Soloist documentation:
.UR https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/soloist
.UE
